alex 3.2.7.4 (Hackage tarball), built with mhs for ghc66/alexchain.nix: the
one source change. MicroHs has no DatatypeContexts, and the context on RSet
constrains nothing (every function on RSet carries its own).

The rest is outside the source: alexchain/shims/ (Data.Map with what alex 3
needs beyond common/shims', Data.IntMap, Data.Array.Base's unsafeRead), and
-D__GLASGOW_HASKELL__=810 with -D'MIN_VERSION_base(a,b,c)=1', so the code
takes its modern-base branches (Control.Exception.bracketOnError,
hSetEncoding utf8, Semigroup) and the generated Scan.hs its Data.Array ones.

--- a/src/Data/Ranged/RangedSet.hs
+++ b/src/Data/Ranged/RangedSet.hs
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@

 -- | An RSet (for Ranged Set) is a list of ranges.  The ranges must be sorted
 -- and not overlap.
-newtype DiscreteOrdered v => RSet v = RSet {rSetRanges :: [Range v]}
+newtype RSet v = RSet {rSetRanges :: [Range v]}
    deriving (Eq, Show, Ord)

 #if MIN_VERSION_base(4,9,0)
